---
title: "I'd consider myself unemployable now"
description: "I didn't get worse at work. I got addicted to owning the outcome."
date: "2026-07-22"
tags:
  - founding
  - algility
published: true
layout: docs
---

I'd consider myself unemployable now.

Not because I can't ship. Because I won't rent my hours to someone else's roadmap and call it a career.

Here's what happened. Algility got loud. Partners. Calls. Flights. SF on the calendar. I kept calling it a side hustle so I could stay comfortable. Comfort was lying to me.

The month I went full-time, volume hit a peak. That wasn't a coincidence. Attention compounds when you stop splitting it.

A job sells you safety. A company sells you ownership. One pays you to solve their problem. The other pays you only if you solve yours.

I still write code. I still take the ugly calls. Difference is simple: if it breaks, it's on me. If it prints, it's on me.

I didn't become unemployable by failing at work. I became unemployable by tasting a game where the scoreboard is mine.
